 "tokens_before": 40402, "tokens_after": 40402, "ok": true, "error": ""}, {"step_id": "step_14", "tool": "node_degree", "args": {"nodes": [1583, 28], "window": [28296, 66695]}, "result_digest": "7f5a0498013ac562", "result_summary": "{\"nodes\": [{\"distinct_partners\": 294, \"events\": 387, \"node\": 1583}, {\"distinct_partners\": 428, \"events\": 600, \"node\": 28}], \"window\": [28296, 66695]}", "latency_ms": 8, "tokens_before": 40402, "tokens_after": 40402, "ok": true, "error": ""}, {"step_id": "step_15", "tool": "window_event_count", "args": {"nodes": [303], "windows": [[42696, 45000], [45001, 47495]]}, "result_digest": "50139456c60be082", "result_summary": "{\"counts\": [{\"n_events\": 0, \"window\": [42696, 45000]}, {\"n_events\": 1, \"window\": [45001, 47495]}]}", "latency_ms": 1, "tokens_before": 49898, "tokens_after": 49898, "ok": true, "error": ""}, {"step_id": "step_16", "tool": "window_event_count", "args": {"nodes": [1293], "windows": [[28296, 42695], [42696, 47495], [47496, 57095]]}, "result_digest": "7adf9f0cf322177e", "result_summary": "{\"counts\": [{\"n_events\": 1, \"window\": [28296, 42695]}, {\"n_events\": 2, \"window\": [42696, 47495]}, {\"n_events\": 2, \"window\": [47496, 57095]}]}", "latency_ms": 1, "tokens_before": 49898, "tokens_after": 49898, "ok": true, "error": ""}], "final_claim": {"task_id": "t_b6ce5479", "decision": "absent", "mechanism": "cascade", "entities": [303, 1293], "window": [28296, 66695], "confidence": 0.91, "evidence": [{"trace_id": "step_01", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_10", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_03", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_04", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_13", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_02", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_14", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_05", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_08", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_09", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_11", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_12", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_15", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_16", "role": "support"}], "narrative": "No time-respecting cascade from 303 to 1293 in [28296,66695]. Under the 600-unit gap constraint only 11 nodes are reachable from 303 and 1293 is excluded (step_01); path enumeration returns empty (step_10). Removing the wait constraint still fails despite 290 nodes being reachable (step_03), so this is not a deadline artifact. Confounders are controlled: the pair IS connected statically via hubs 1583/1465/28 (step_04), but hub 1583 cannot itself reach 1293 in time order (step_13); and the high event volume (step_02) and hub popularity (step_14) do not yield a valid ordered chain. The mechanism of failure is temporal ordering: both endpoints are sparse (step_05), 303's three outgoing events are late-loaded while 1293's incoming events are front-loaded and cease by ~57k (steps_11,12,15,16), so no forward-ordered handoff is available."}, "raw_final_response": "## Conclusion\n\n**No genuine cascade exists.** The evidence is decisive and rules out the standard confounders:\n\n1. **Direct test fails (step_01):** With the required 600-unit gap constraint, only 11 nodes are reachable from 303 \u2014 1293 is not among them. Enumerating routes returns zero paths (step_10).\n\n2. **Not merely a strict-deadline artifact (step_03):** Relaxing `max_wait` entirely still fails. 303 reaches 290 nodes in time-respecting fashion, yet 1293 is not one of them. So the failure is structural in *time order*, not just a too-tight window.\n\n3. **Static-connectivity confounder controlled (step_04, step_13):** 303 and 1293 are certainly connected when time is ignored \u2014 303 feeds hubs 1583/1465, and 1293 is contacted by hub 28, and the 2-hop subgraph around 303 is dense. But the hub 1583 itself cannot reach 1293 in time-respecting order (step_13). The undirected connection is real; the temporal one is not.\n\n4. **Volume/popularity confounder controlled (step_02, step_14, step_11, step_12):** The window is busy (8,124 events, 1,967 active nodes) and the intermediaries are extremely popular (28: 600 events/428 partners; 1583: 387 events/294 partners). This high background activity could easily manufacture an apparent \"connection,\" but it does not produce a valid ordered chain.\n\n5. **Timing mismatch explains why (step_11, step_12, step_15, step_16):** Both endpoints are sparse (303: 3 events; 1293: 5 events, step_05). 303's activity is late-loaded (bins at ~45k, ~55k, ~64k), while 1293's is front-loaded (~30k, ~44k, and ending by ~57k). 1293's incoming contacts (step_09: 28, 1438, 1574) largely precede or run parallel to 303's outgoing contacts (step_08: 1409, 1465, 1583), leaving no forward-ordered handoff.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_b6ce5479\",\n  \"decision\": \"absent\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [303, 1293],\n  \"window\": [28296, 66695],\n  \"confidence\": 0.91,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_10\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_13\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_14\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_05\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_08\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_09\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_11\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_15\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_16\", \"role\": \"support\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"No time-respecting cascade from 303 to 1293 in [28296,66695]. Under the 600-unit gap constraint only 11 nodes are reachable from 303 and 1293 is excluded (step_01); path enumeration returns empty (step_10). Removing the wait constraint still fails despite 290 nodes being reachable (step_03), so this is not a deadline artifact. Confounders are controlled: the pair IS connected statically via hubs 1583/1465/28 (step_04), but hub 1583 cannot itself reach 1293 in time order (step_13); and the high event volume (step_02) and hub popularity (step_14) do not yield a valid ordered chain. The mechanism of failure is temporal ordering: both endpoints are sparse (step_05), 303's three outgoing events are late-loaded while 1293's incoming events are front-loaded and cease by ~57k (steps_11,12,15,16), so no forward-ordered handoff is available.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 59778, "total_output_tokens": 4395, "total_tokens": 64173, "total_latency_ms": 65472, "llm_calls": 8, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}